# The trial of pod-enter in podvm (T-059), at podvm main cb57d4b (commit).
# The patch applies alone, and after pod-guest.patch with git apply --3way:
# the two patches change the same tag lines in the same way, and only the
# rows of docs/runtime-state.md that each adds conflict (keep both rows).
# crates/podvm-enter
# keeps podvm's glue and re-exports the crate: NAMES (PODVM_MODE,
# PODVM_ACTIVE_MODE, PODVM_CACHE, PODVM_MAPS, PODVM_LIB_PATH,
# PODVM_DEVICE_SPEC, PODVM_DEVICE_FDS, the cache marker
# .podvm-cache-complete, the memfd label podvm-payload), docker's codes of
# podvm-probe's exit and the trait ExitCode (125 for a runtime error),
# runtime(text), GUEST_EXE_VAR, and each function that takes the names with
# podvm's signature (ladder::choose, ladder::parse_mode, memfd::stage,
# memfd::probe::answer, device::{specs_of, push_spec, push_serve,
# banner_line, SPEC_VAR, SERVE_VAR}, userland::{userland_maps_table,
# host_env, MAPS_VAR, LIB_PATH_VAR}, stage::stage_cache, ns_fallback_line).
# 27 files leave podvm. Each Plan gets names: NAMES; Plan::env_for takes
# &NAMES; a runtime error of podvm is podvm_enter::runtime(text). The gate's
# pin of tty_refusal goes (the test moves), document-state names Mode in
# pod-enter, and the citations of the moved files name pod-enter. Each
# podcrates tag moves to v0.9.0, with the tags of podvm-supervise.
# podvm's tests of the touched crates and the integration tests that enter
# or refuse; clippy of the workspace and rustfmt of the touched crates, as
# podvm's gate.yml runs them; the runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate;
# each Rust toolchain of the workflows against the rust-version of
# podcrates; and the binary `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static
# check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-enter
cargo test -q -p podvm-supervise
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
cargo test -q -p podvm --test detached_stdio
cargo test -q -p podvm --test qol
cargo test -q -p podvm --test curated_refusals
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-enter -p podvm-supervise -p podvm -p podvm-gate -p podvm-release --check
cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-enter, pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-term and pod-tls at 0.9.0); the
# trial's path form has no row for them. Each other row of the patch must be
# the generated one.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
